  <model metaid="meta_talinolol_liver" id="talinolol_liver" name="Model for talinolol elimination in the liver" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for talinolol elimination in the liver</h1>
        <p>Model for the hepatic uptake and biliary excretion of talinolol in
<a href="http://sbml.org">SBML</a>.
Talinolol is not metabolized (the metabolites in the urine are 0.33 % of
the dose, Trausch1995), it is taken up into the liver (OATP1B1, <code>TALIM</code>)
and excreted unchanged into the bile (P-glycoprotein, <code>TALEX</code>). The bile
reaches the duodenum (<code>TALEHC</code>, the enterohepatic circulation); the bile
collected by a T-drain after a cholecystectomy is not (<code>f_EHC</code> 0).</p>
        <ul>
          <li>enterohepatic circulation (see Terhaag1989); &quot;The biliary clearance amounted to 43 ml/hr/kg (range: 13-212 ml/hr/kg).&quot;</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
